# Frontend runtime API base URL
#
# This MUST point at your deployed Django backend on any real deployment
# (e.g. Vercel). Leaving it unset/relative only works for local `vite dev`,
# which proxies /api to the Django dev server (see vite.config.js). On a
# static host like Vercel there is no such proxy, so a relative value here
# gets silently caught by the SPA rewrite and register/login will look like
# they "succeed" while never reaching the backend.
#
# Local dev example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

# Production example (set this in your Vercel project's Environment Variables):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend-domain/api
